cff-version: 1.2.0
title: VinaMetalic
message: >-
  If you use VinaMetalic in your work, please cite this software and the
  AutoDock Vina / AutoDock4Zn publications it builds upon.
type: software
authors:
  - family-names: Yaranga Nana
    given-names: Christian
    orcid: "https://orcid.org/0009-0000-5539-0526"
    affiliation: "Universidad Norbert Wiener"
version: 1.0.0
date-released: "2026-10-21"
license: Apache-2.0
repository-code: "https://github.com/cristhianyaranganana-arch/VinaMetalic"
url: "https://github.com/cristhianyaranganana-arch/VinaMetalic"
abstract: >-
  VinaMetalic is a fork of AutoDock Vina 1.2.7 with native metal coordination
  scoring for metalloenzymes: an AutoDock4-style 12-6 metal-donor pair term, a
  coordination-number penalty and a bounded geometry bonus, all with analytic
  gradients, plus automatic detection of the receptor-bound coordination
  occupancy. With no parametrized metal in the receptor, scoring and output are
  byte-identical to AutoDock Vina 1.2.7.
keywords:
  - molecular docking
  - metalloenzymes
  - metal coordination
  - virtual screening
  - computational chemistry
  - drug discovery
